    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 6 USER]\ne048\tThe team could support a public beta for eight weeks if we rotate office hours, but the senior maintainer will be on leave during the last three weeks.\ne049\tPriya says that is fine because it forces knowledge sharing.\ne050\tHe says it turns his absence into an experiment other people did not choose.\ne051\tWe can move the date, but then we miss a workshop where many potential users will be together.\ne052\tThe workshop is a real learning opportunity, not only publicity.\n[Turn 6 ASSISTANT]\ne053\tLaunching into a known reduction in experienced support is a real risk, and calling it knowledge sharing does not assign the work.\ne054\tThe workshop also offers unusually concentrated feedback.\ne055\tOne compromise is to use the workshop as an announced hands-on preview and schedule the public beta after the maintainer returns.\ne056\tThat preserves some learning while delaying open access, though contributors may reasonably see it as another preview and workshop participants may still form expectations.",
